 # SoproSynth

-SoproSynth is a flat-layout Python library providing a backend-neutral request/result API for the upstream Sopro V2 Turbo text-to-speech system. The native upstream Sopro implementation is the default and reference backend. The stable public request API is version 1; optional ONNXVoice integration is a separate, explicitly selected backend.
+SoproSynth provides a stable Python request/result API around ONNXVoice's built-in Sopro V2 Turbo implementation. SoproSynth owns request validation, reference-voice lifecycle, loudness calibration policy, result metadata, and WAV output. ONNXVoice owns Sopro model assets, tokenization, graph/session execution, and inference.

-SoproSynth accepts a single text request at a time. Callers retain ownership of text preparation, segment boundaries, composition, and final mastering. Python >=3.10 is required.
+SoproSynth supports one synthesis path: ONNXVoice's Sopro adapter. It does not vendor model weights or implement ONNX inference itself. Python 3.10 or newer is required.

-## Support status
+## Support boundary

-| Area                              | Status                                                                 |
-| --------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |
-| Native Sopro synthesis            | Primary backend; requires the `native` extra and upstream model assets |
-| Strict request/result API         | Stable SoproSynth API v1                                               |
-| Reference voice preparation/reuse | Supported within one open runtime                                      |
-| Native streaming                  | Supported by the native backend only                                   |
-| Static voice-level calibration    | Opt-in; no calibration records are bundled                             |
-| ONNXVoice Sopro integration       | Optional and experimental; see [ONNX status](#onnx-status)             |
-| ONNX streaming                    | Not supported                                                          |
+| Capability           | v0.1.0 support                                            |
+| -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |
+| Model                | `sopro:v2-turbo`                                          |
+| Profile              | `wasm-uint8`                                              |
+| Provider             | CPU (`CPUExecutionProvider`)                              |
+| Languages            | `en`, `pt`, `fr`, `de`, and `auto`                        |
+| Input                | One text request and a prepared reference voice           |
+| Output               | Mono float32 PCM at 24 kHz; `save_wav()` writes PCM16 WAV |
+| Prepared voice reuse | Supported within the same open runtime                    |
+| Request measurement  | Supported through ONNXVoice text preparation              |
+| Streaming            | Not supported                                             |

-Offline unit and boundary tests use fake backends. They do not establish quality or model-level parity for a real Sopro model.
+Unsupported profiles and providers fail explicitly. SoproSynth does not perform language detection, text segmentation, pronunciation overrides, linguistic-token processing, word alignment, or final mastering.

